.TH std::nullopt 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::nullopt \- std::nullopt

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <optional>
inline constexpr nullopt_t nullopt{/*unspecified*/};  \fI(since C++17)\fP

std::nullopt is a constant of type std::nullopt_t. Used to indicate that an std::optional
does not contain a value.

.SH See also

nullopt_t indicator of an std::optional that does not contain a value
\fI(C++17)\fP   \fI(class)\fP
